Secrets Management in GitHub Actions

Today I learned how to handle secrets securely in GitHub Actions so sensitive values never appear in code or logs.

🔹 GitHub Secrets
GitHub Secrets are encrypted values used in workflows for:
API keys
Tokens
Passwords
Cloud credentials
They are accessed securely during workflow execution.

🔹 Repository vs Environment Secrets
Repository secrets apply to all workflows in a repo
Environment secrets apply only to a specific environment (like dev/prod)
Environment secrets support extra controls like approvals
This helps maintain separation between environments.

🔹 Using Secrets Securely
Never hardcode secrets in YAML
Avoid printing secrets in logs
Use least privilege credentials
Restrict access to protected branches

🔥 3-Line Takeaway
Secrets protect sensitive data.
 Scopes control access.
 Safe usage prevents leaks.
